   dphi/dn = 0 for the phase field (a 90° contact angle where ice
   meets the wall), zero heat flux for T (insulating), and zero
   vapor flux for rho_v (sealed — no mass enters or leaves there).

   Wall               phi_i (ice)            T (temperature)          rho_v (vapor)
   ------------------ ---------------------- ------------------------ ------------------------
   x = 0   (left)     Neumann  dphi/dn=0     Neumann  (insulating)    Neumann  (sealed)
   x = Lx  (right)    Neumann  dphi/dn=0     Neumann  (insulating)    Neumann  (sealed)
   y = 0   (bottom)   regolith  theta=0.0°  Neumann  (insulating)    Neumann  (sealed)
   y = Ly  (top)      regolith  theta=0.0°  Neumann  (insulating)    Neumann  (sealed)

   phi_i is never pinned (no Dirichlet path exists for it). On a
   face marked "regolith" above, its NATURAL condition is the wall
   free-energy term  dphi/dn = cos(theta)*phi(1-phi)/eps  rather than
   zero. A face marked "open" imposes nothing on phi_i: the ice
   passes through it. Any other face keeps dphi/dn = 0 (a 90°
   contact angle).
